# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.
#
# WHERE EACH ENVIRONMENT GETS THESE
#
#   Local      this file, copied to .env.local. For the local Supabase stack,
#              run `supabase start` from Journeyman/ and use the values it
#              prints -- they are fixed dev defaults, identical for everyone,
#              and are not secrets.
#   Preview    Vercel -> Settings -> Environment Variables, scoped to Preview.
#              Points at the preview Supabase project, never production.
#   Production Vercel, scoped to Production only.
#
# The anon (publishable) key is designed to be public -- it is protected by row
# level security, and it ships in the JavaScript bundle either way.
#
# NEVER add the service_role / secret key here, and never give any variable a
# REACT_APP_ prefix unless it is safe in public: Create React App inlines every
# REACT_APP_* value into the client bundle at build time. The service role key
# bypasses row level security entirely and belongs only to the server.

REACT_APP_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
REACT_APP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-publishable-key-here
